-- title:
--   Cotangent–congruence length inequality at cube-free levels
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be an odd prime, let $W$ be a Weierstrass model over $\mathbf{Z}$ with $\Delta\neq 0$ which is semistable in the sense that every prime $q$ with $q\mid\Delta$ satisfies $q\nmid c_4$, and assume the $p$-torsion of $W$ over $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ is nontrivial with no Galois-stable $\mathbf{Z}/p$-submodule other than $0$ and itself. Let $M_0\geq 1$ be a level at which $W$ is residually modular mod $p$, i.e. there are a normalised weight-$2$ eigenform on $\Gamma_0(M_0)$ and a maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ of the integral closure of $\mathbf{Z}$ in $\mathbf{C}$ containing $p$ such that, for every prime $\ell\nmid\Delta M_0$ with $\ell\neq p$, the $\ell$-th $q$-coefficient is integral and congruent to $a_\ell(W)=\#(\mathbf{Z}/\ell)+1-\#W(\mathbf{Z}/\ell)$ modulo $\mathfrak m$; assume $p^2\nmid M_0$ and $q^3\nmid M_0$ for every prime $q\neq p$. Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring which is a domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field and $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes with $p\in S$ containing every prime dividing $\Delta$, and let $N\geq 1$ satisfy: every prime factor of $N$ lies in $S$; $q^2\mid N$ and $q^3\nmid N$ for every $q\in S$ with $q\neq p$; if $p\mid\Delta$ or $p\nmid a_p(W)$ then $p\mid N$ and $p^2\nmid N$; if $p\nmid\Delta$ and $p\mid a_p(W)$ then $p\nmid N$. Assume the weight-$2$ cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ are spanned over $\mathbf{C}$ by those with integral $q$-expansion coefficients, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbf{Z}$-subalgebra of endomorphisms generated by the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, and the $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$) to the residue field of $\mathcal O$ with $\theta(T_\ell)$ the residue of $a_\ell(W)$ for all primes $\ell\nmid N$ outside $S$. Then there is a complete discrete valuation ring $\mathcal O'$, a domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field, finite as an $\mathcal O$-module via a local and injective structure map, and an $\mathcal O'$-algebra homomorphism $\pi_T$ from the localised Hecke algebra $T=$ [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪' θ'`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) (the localisation of the $\mathcal O'$-Hecke base algebra at the prime attached to the character $\theta'$ obtained from $\theta$ by the induced map of residue fields) to $\mathcal O'$, with the following property: for every proof that the $p$-torsion of $W_{\mathbf{Q}}$ over $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ has cardinality $p^2$ and that its Galois action factors through a finite extension of $\mathbf{Q}$, every ring homomorphism $\iota:\mathbf{Z}/p\to$ residue field of $\mathcal O'$, and every Hecke–Galois representation datum $H$ over $T$ for $(N,S,\mathcal O',\theta')$, both of the following hold. First, if $p\mid\Delta$ or $p\nmid a_p(W)$, then for every universal deformation datum $D$ of the residual representation $\bar\rho_{W,p}$ base-changed along $\iota$ for the ordinary condition [`GaloisRep.ordinaryCondition 𝒪' p S`](def/GaloisRep_LocalConditions.html#L28) (cyclotomic determinant, ordinary at $p$, unramified outside $S$), every local $\mathcal O'$-algebra map $\varphi:D.R\to T$ such that the base change of $D.\rho$ along $\varphi$ is equivalent to $H.\rho$ satisfies $$\operatorname{length}_{\mathcal O'}\big(\ker(\pi_T\circ\varphi)/\ker(\pi_T\circ\varphi)^2\big)\ \leq\ \operatorname{length}_{\mathcal O'}\big(\mathcal O'/\pi_T(\operatorname{ann}\ker\pi_T)\big).$$ Secondly, the same inequality holds, with the flat condition [`GaloisRep.flatCondition 𝒪' p S`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L47) in place of the ordinary one, when $p\nmid\Delta$ and $p\mid a_p(W)$.
--
--   This is Wiles's numerical criterion inequality in the form used in Taylor–Wiles patching: the cotangent module of the kernel of the induced map on the deformation ring is bounded in length by the congruence module of the localised Hecke algebra, in the minimal ordinary case and in the flat case at $p$, for Taylor–Wiles levels $N$ whose exponents away from $p$ are exactly $2$ and for a residual-modularity witness level $M_0$ that is not divisible by $p^2$ and is cube-free away from $p$. It feeds the construction of a finite extension of $\mathcal O$ carrying simultaneously a Hecke–Galois representation datum and a patching datum, from which the isomorphism of the deformation ring with the Hecke algebra is deduced.
